            <ArticleTitle>Angioplasty of a large aortocoronary bypass graft utilizing a single oversized balloon catheter.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Angioplasty of large saphenous vein grafts may present problems because of unavailability of adequately sized balloon dilatation catheters. We report a case of successful PTCA of a left anterior descending graft by using a 5 mm balloon and a standard 8F guiding catheter.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
